# .trivyignore — accept ONLY what cannot be fixed, each with a reason + review date.
# Anything fixable (undici, etc.) is fixed in code/image and does NOT belong here.

# AVD-DS-0026 (LOW): Dockerfile without HEALTHCHECK.
# Reason: the healthcheck is defined at the orchestration layer — docker-compose (app/nginx),
#   and, under Kubernetes, liveness/readiness probes (a Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK is ignored under k8s).
#   Duplicating it in the Dockerfile = redundant.
# Accepted: 2026-06-23. Review: when Kubernetes probes are introduced — confirm they cover this.
AVD-DS-0026

# CVE-2026-14456 (HIGH): libssl3 / libcrypto3 3.5.7-r0 in the node:24-alpine3.24 base.
# Reason: fixed by Alpine in 3.5.8-r0, but the base image has not been rebuilt yet — there is
#   nothing to patch from this repository. `apk upgrade` here would report clean without changing
#   what the app actually uses: node is not linked against these libraries at all
#   (`ldd $(which node)` -> musl, libstdc++, libgcc only), it carries its own OpenSSL.
# Actual exploitability: the sole dynamic consumer in the image is busybox `ssl_client`, reached
#   only by `wget https://`. Nothing in the runtime does that — the health check is plain HTTP on
#   loopback. Note node reports openssl 3.5.7 as well, so its bundled copy may carry the same
#   defect; that is a base-image rebuild, not an apk upgrade.
# Accepted: 2026-08-29. Review: 2026-09-30, or sooner — drop this line once the base image ships
#   3.5.8-r0 and confirm the scan is green without it.
CVE-2026-14456

